  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates the most favorable outcome among those with the minimum probability in each lottery and prefers the lottery with the better such outcome. However, the individual focuses on the 75% chance of no loss — a highly probable outcome — and prefers Lottery A because of this. This is the opposite of focusing on the least probable outcomes. The individual does not consider rare events or compare outcomes based on their low probability. Instead, they prioritize a high-probability favorable outcome. There is no alignment with the decision reason in terms of information considered (least probable outcomes) or the rule (preferring the more favorable rare outcome). The reasoning is based on a different principle entirely — favoring high probability of no loss over complexity or multiple losses.",
